  "notes": "{遺伝|いでん} refers to the biological process of passing traits from parents to offspring. Used both as a noun and with する to mean 'to be hereditary.'\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {遺伝|いでん}{子|し}: gene\n- {遺伝|いでん}{情報|じょうほう}: genetic information\n- {遺伝|いでん}{病|びょう}: hereditary disease\n- {遺伝|いでん}{子|し}{検査|けんさ}: genetic testing\n- {遺伝|いでん}{学|がく}: genetics (the field of study)\n- {遺伝|いでん}{子|し}{組|く}み{換|か}え: genetic modification/GMO\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {遺伝|いでん}する: to be hereditary\n- {親|おや}から{遺伝|いでん}する: to inherit from one's parents\n- {遺伝|いでん}の{影響|えいきょう}: influence of heredity\n\nUSAGE:\nIn everyday conversation, often used when discussing traits like appearance or health conditions that run in families.",
